res many convenience  stores and gas stations  so that helped propel its growth and  jewel also marketed it they  gave jewel packages to celebrities for  as little as a dollar  to try to get them to use it and be seen  using it in the hopes that  celebrities and other social media  influencers would help spread the word  as joule's own data would later disclose  some of the customers its product was  attracting  had never smoked cigarettes before by  the end of 2018  jewel labs had captured 68 percent of  the 1.9  billion dollar u.s e-cigarette market  prominent investors took notice  a fundraising ground that summer brought  the startup's value to about 16 billion  dollars  but 2018 was also the year jewel found  itself in the crosshairs of regulators  the food and drug administration opened  an investigation into jewel  after parents and school administrators  sounded the alarm about  youth vaping after two decades of  declining teen cigarette smoking  a 2018 survey revealed that the share of  high schoolers who were vaping had  increased significantly  when the regulator in charge of  the e-cigarette industry targets  your company that's a big deal  and jewel took a series of steps that  year to try to show  that they were taking the problem  seriously the first thing they did was  they said that they would work with  retailers  to ensure that at the point of sale  kids weren't getting access to jewel and  other e-cigarettes  but the fda wasn't satisfied it  conducted an inspection at the company's  headquarters  and the agency threatened to take  flavored e-cigarettes off the market  entirely because they were attracting  underage users jewel responded  by voluntarily pulling most of their  sweet and fruity flavors  out of brick and mortar retail stores so  those flavors  included mango cucumber and creme brulee  for example jewel also suspended its  social media marketing  in the u.s despite all this jules  valuation  soared to 38 billion dollars when altria  the maker of marlborough bought a  significant minority stake in the  company  altria wanted to get a piece of the  growing e-cigarette market  and ultra's own e-cigarette products  were not that successful  altria got in at an inauspicious moment  after making the nearly 13 billion  dollar investment in jewel  things began to unwind rite aid the  third largest u.s pharmacy chain  announced it would stop  selling e-cigarettes in its stores in  september 2019  jules ceo kevin burns stepped down he  was replaced by altria  executive kc crossweight that same month  in a blow to the company's overseas  ambitions china  the world's biggest tobacco market  halted jules sales  just days after its launch there and in  the u.s governors called for immediate  bans on all flavored e-cigarettes  common sense says if you don't know  what you are smoking don't smoke it  at the same time the entire nicotine  vaping industry faced  a full-blown pr crisis new vaping  numbers  illnesses top 1000 with deaths on the  rise some patients actually suffered  toxic chemical burns  to their lungs and airways as if being  exposed to a chemical spill  after hospitals throughout the country  linked at least eight deaths to vaping  us health officials urged americans to  stop using any and all  e-cigarette products while authorities  investigated the cause  the illnesses were eventually linked to  marijuana vaping devices containing  vitamin e oil  not to e-cigarettes like joule but the  damage to vaping's image  continued to be felt and the tsunami of  bad news for juul  continued jul's new ceo halted most u.s  advertising  then stopped all u.s sales of jewels  sweet and fruity flavors  state attorneys general across the  country sued jewel for  deceptive marketing of its products  jewel basically took a page from big  tobacco's playbook  by marketing its products in a manner  that was appealing to underage youth  in court filings experts allege that  even though the models jewel used and  its 2015 promotional materials were in  their 20s  they appeared in poses and behaviors  more characteristic  of underage teens than mature adults  cross wheat was grilled by lawmakers for  the marketing methods joule employed  before he arrived  we are focused on combating underage  access because i know it puts it all at  risk  if we don't make progress here sir how  do i trust what you say  my actions so far since i've joined um  support our recognition that more needed  to be done more done  with fewer people amid a sharp drop in  sales in the fall of 2020  joule continued to shrink its workforce  down to around a thousand  from its high of just over 4 000 and  pulled out of most overseas markets  and altria wrote down the value of its  staking joule by  around 11 billion dollars everything  hinges  on an fda review that will determine  whether or not jules products can stay  on the market  or whether they have to come off it  presented a real potential for a public  health benefit  um you know getting adult cigarette  smokers off  of cigarettes which kill 480 000  people a year you know offered a lot of  promise it was interesting to investors  it was compelling to public health  experts  but at the same time joule presented an  incredible risk  federal data now show that youth vaping  is decreasing  the ceo said joule is now focused on its  founding principle  to help smokers move away from  cigarettes but that joule needs to prove  it can be trusted  if it can do that crossway said jewel  has a lot of potential in the long  term but that will be an uphill battle
 

